---

<BaseLayout
  title="Brighton & Ipswich 15:00 near Sol — skip Liverpool, Chelsea, United | Dubliners"
  description="Sunday 8 Nov 15:00: Brighton–Brentford and Ipswich–Bournemouth near Sol. Quieter English games if you are not chasing Liverpool, Chelsea or United. Four bars, Maps, ask which screen."
  path={PATH}
  lang="en"
  hreflang={{ en: PATH, es: PATH_ES }}
  ogImage="/images/dubliners-screens-sol-1200.webp"
  extraJsonLd={[articleLd, faqLd]}
>
  <section class="hero hero-compact" data-show-until={SHOW_UNTIL}>
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumb current="Brighton and Ipswich 15:00 — not Liverpool/Chelsea/United" schema />
      <h1>Not chasing Liverpool, Chelsea or United: Brighton–Brentford and Ipswich–Bournemouth at 15:00 near Sol</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Sunday 8 November at 15:00 has four English kick-offs. Two of them will fill the loud rooms:
        Palace–Liverpool and Sunderland–Chelsea. United–Villa is 17:30.
        <strong>If you support Brighton, Brentford, Ipswich or Bournemouth — or you just want a quieter English pint — ask for these two.</strong>
        Meet at the four sister bars by Sol. Named listings: Dubliners What’s On only. Ask which screen.
      </p>
      <p class="small">En español: <a href={withBase(PATH_ES)} hreflang="es" lang="es">Sin perseguir Liverpool, Chelsea ni United: Brighton e Ipswich a las 15:00 junto a Sol</a></p>
      <FanWeekendCtas lang="en" findHref="/visit/" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>These two 15:00s, not the whole Premier block</h2>
      <p>
        Other pages already list all four 15:00s against the 15:30 NFL Game, walk you through which Sunday door if you just woke up,
        and cover United–Villa at 17:30. The old Brighton page is Getafe on Thursday — not today.
        This page is only for fans <strong>who are not chasing Liverpool, Chelsea or United</strong>
        and want Brighton vs Brentford or Ipswich Town vs Bournemouth at 15:00.
        Saturday’s meetup is finished. Do not treat this as a Liverpool/Chelsea capture page.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>15:00</strong> — Brighton vs Brentford (Dubliners <a href={withBase('/whats-on/')}>What’s On</a>)</li>
        <li><strong>15:00</strong> — Ipswich Town vs Bournemouth (same board)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Palace–Liverpool and Sunderland–Chelsea kick off at the same hour; they will hog screens. Say the two quieter names when you sit down.
        United–Villa at 17:30 is later if you stay — it is not this page’s job.
      </p>

      <h2>Four-bar meeting point — ask which screen</h2>
      <p>
        The meeting point is four doors, not one recinto. We do not claim O’Reilly’s, O’Connell’s or Four Corner show Brighton or Ipswich.
        Named Brighton–Brentford and Ipswich–Bournemouth listings sit on Dubliners’ What’s On (Espoz y Mina 7, from 12:00).
        Four Corner opens 14:00 with sports screens — one hour before 15:00; not open before 14:00; ask which game is on.
        O’Reilly’s (Matheu 4, usual from 11:30) and O’Connell’s (Espoz y Mina 7, from 12:00 today): ask at the door.
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>O’Reilly’s Restaurant Bar — Pasaje de Matheu 4, 28012 Madrid.</strong>
          Terrace restaurant-bar. Meeting point before 15:00. We do not list its board.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.oreillys} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.oreillys} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Dubliners — Calle de Espoz y Mina 7, 28012 Madrid.</strong>
          Sunday from 12:00. Brighton vs Brentford and Ipswich Town vs Bournemouth are on What’s On. Ask which screen — not every game on every screen.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.dubliners} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.dubliners} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>O’Connell’s — Calle de Espoz y Mina 7, 28012 Madrid</strong> (Maps listing: O’Connell St).
          Same street number, different door. From 12:00 today (usual Sunday 14:00). Meeting point; we do not copy Dubliners’ board here.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.oconnell} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.oconnell} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Four Corner — Calle de la Victoria 6, 28012 Madrid.</strong>
          Opens 14:00 until late · sports screens. Not open before 14:00. We do not list which game it shows. Ask.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.fourCorner} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.fourCorner} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>NFL and Atleti sit alongside — do not substitute</h2>
      <p>
        These two quieter 15:00s do not replace the rest of Sunday.
        NFL afternoon/evening sits alongside (Bengals vs Falcons 15:30 LIVE at Dubliners; more from 19:00 on What’s On).
        Atlético vs Barcelona 21:00 is on the same Dubliners board.
        Coordinate the screens; do not treat Brighton or Ipswich as a reason to skip the NFL or Atleti rooms, and do not treat those as a reason to hide the quieter English games.
      </p>

      <OriginalFourBars lang="en" when="sunday" findHref="/visit/" />

      <h2>FAQ</h2>
      <dl class="faq">
        <dt><strong>Not chasing Liverpool, Chelsea or United. Which 15:00s?</strong></dt>
        <dd>Brighton vs Brentford and Ipswich Town vs Bournemouth. On Dubliners What’s On. Ask which screen. Meet at the four bars.</dd>
        <dt><strong>Where do I meet?</strong></dt>
        <dd>Four Corner Victoria 6 from 14:00 (sports screens, not before). O’Reilly’s Matheu 4. Dubliners and O’Connell’s Espoz y Mina 7. Maps above.</dd>
        <dt><strong>Do these replace NFL or Atleti–Barça?</strong></dt>
        <dd>No. Coordinate. NFL from 15:30 / 19:00 and Atleti 21:00 sit alongside. United–Villa 17:30 is later if you stay.</dd>
      </dl>

      <LinkHub
        heading="h2"
        groups={[
